{{^hasQueue}}<p class="hint">This server has no queue running.</p>{{/hasQueue}}
{{#hasQueue}}
<h2>Addresses</h2>
<table>
  <thead><tr><th>state</th><th class="num">members</th><th class="num">places</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>{{#states}}<tr class="{{#stuck}}warn{{/stuck}}">
    <td>{{label}}</td><td class="num">{{members}}</td><td class="num">{{places}}</td>
  </tr>{{/states}}</tbody>
</table>
{{#retrying}}<p class="hint">{{.}} could not be looked up because the service did not answer.
  Nothing is wrong with those addresses and nobody needs to do anything: they are tried again on
  their own, 15 minutes after the first failure and then an hour, four hours and a day.</p>{{/retrying}}
{{#stuck}}<p class="hint warn">{{.}} address(es) came back as <strong>no such place</strong>
  from {{service}}. Those are not retried on their own &mdash; asking the same service the same
  question tomorrow gets the same answer, every day, forever. They are looked at again when the
  address is edited, when this server is pointed at a different geocoding service, or when somebody
  presses <em>try the given-up-on ones again</em>.</p>{{/stuck}}

<table class="bars">
  <tr><th>waiting</th>
    <td class="w"><span class="bar" style="width:{{share}}%"></span></td>
    <td class="n">{{depth}} of {{capacity}}</td></tr>
</table>
{{#full}}<p class="problem">The queue is full. Anything asked for now is refused rather than
  queued &mdash; which is recorded below, so nothing disappears quietly.</p>{{/full}}

<table>
  <tbody>
    <tr><th>geocoding</th><td>{{geocoding}}</td></tr>
    <tr><th>pace</th><td>one every {{gap}} seconds, across everything this machine asks</td></tr>
    <tr><th>next</th><td>{{#inFlight}}asking now: <span class="mono">{{.}}</span>{{/inFlight}}{{^inFlight}}{{#nextIn}}in about {{.}} second(s){{/nextIn}}{{^nextIn}}ready{{/nextIn}}{{/inFlight}}</td></tr>
    {{#backoff}}<tr><th>backing off</th><td class="warn">waiting {{backoffFor}} more second(s) before asking anything else. {{lastProblem}}</td></tr>{{/backoff}}
    {{^backoff}}<tr><th>backoff</th><td class="dim">none. A failure would cost {{backoffNext}} second(s), doubling each time.</td></tr>{{/backoff}}
    <tr><th>running</th><td>{{#running}}yes{{/running}}{{^running}}<span class="warn">no</span>{{/running}}</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<table>
  <thead><tr><th>asked</th><th class="num">placed</th><th class="num">no answer</th><th class="num">failed</th><th class="num">given up</th><th class="num">refused</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody><tr>
    <td class="num">{{accepted}}</td>
    <td class="num">{{answered}}</td>
    <td class="num dim">{{nothing}}</td>
    <td class="num dim">{{failed}}</td>
    <td class="num">{{abandoned}}</td>
    <td class="num">{{refused}}</td>
  </tr></tbody>
</table>
<p class="hint"><strong>No answer</strong> is the service saying it has never heard of that address,
  which is a correct answer and costs nothing. <strong>Failed</strong> is the service not answering
  at all, which is what starts a backoff; a job is tried {{attempts}} times before it is given up
  on.</p>
{{#wantsContact}}<p class="hint warn">Nominatim's policy asks for a way to reach whoever runs this
  server, and this one has not been told. Set <span class="mono">gps.contact</span> in
  <span class="mono">config.cfg</span> &mdash; an email address is enough. A client that cannot be
  reached can be blocked without warning, and from in here that looks exactly like geocoding
  quietly stopping.</p>{{/wantsContact}}

<h2>Lately</h2>
{{^anyRecent}}<p class="hint">Nothing has been asked for this community yet.</p>{{/anyRecent}}
{{#anyRecent}}
<table>
  <thead><tr><th>what</th><th>how it went</th><th class="num">tries</th><th class="num">took</th><th>when</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>{{#recent}}<tr>
    <td class="mono">{{label}}</td>
    <td class="{{#good}}good{{/good}}{{#bad}}bad{{/bad}}">{{outcome}}{{#detail}} <span class="dim">&mdash; {{.}}</span>{{/detail}}</td>
    <td class="num dim">{{attempts}}</td>
    <td class="num dim">{{millis}}ms</td>
    <td class="dim">{{ago}} ago</td>
  </tr>{{/recent}}</tbody>
</table>
{{/anyRecent}}
{{/hasQueue}}
